{
  "title": "An In-Context Learning Agent for Formal Theorem-Proving",
  "authors": [
    "Amitayush Thakur",
    "George Tsoukalas",
    "Yeming Wen",
    "Jimmy Xin",
    "Swarat Chaudhuri"
  ],
  "year": 2024,
  "arxivId": "2310.04353",
  "abstract": "This paper introduces C OPRA, an in-context learning agent for formal theorem-proving. C OPRA uses a high-capacity language model to propose tactic applications in a stateful backtracking search, outperforming few-shot invocations and finetuned approaches in Lean and Coq proof environments.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "Imagine having a **personal proof assistant** that can help you discover formal proofs in mathematics. The key idea behind C OPRA is to use a **high-capacity language model** to guide a **stateful backtracking search**. This approach allows the agent to learn from its interactions with the proof environment and adapt to new problems.",
